If labels are [3,2,1,2]: edges: (2,3),(1,2),(1,2),(2,3) → 2 distinct. Still not 4.

Try [1,2,3,4]: edges (1,2),(2,3),(3,4),(1,4) → all distinct dominoes → 4. Yes!

Sample 4: 7 vertices complete graph, answer 16. With 7 vertices and labels 1-6, by pigeonhole two vertices share a label. Those two vertices' edge uses domino (x,x). The 21 edges, but some share dominoes. Max is 16.

So the algorithm is: try all 6^n label assignments, for each count distinct domino types across all edges, take the maximum.

6^7 = 279936, and m≤21, so this is very fast.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace ConsoleApp1
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string[] input = Console.ReadLine().Split(' ');
            int v = Convert.ToInt32(input[0]);
            int e = Convert.ToInt32(input[1]);

            int[] eu = new int[e];
            int[] ev = new int[e];

            for (int i = 0; i < e; ++i)
            {
                input = Console.ReadLine().Split(' ');
                eu[i] = Convert.ToInt32(input[0]) - 1;
                ev[i] = Convert.ToInt32(input[1]) - 1;
            }

            int[] label = new int[v];
            int best = 0;

            // Try all 6^v assignments
            int total = 1;
            for (int i = 0; i < v; i++) total *= 6;

            for (int mask = 0; mask < total; mask++)
            {
                int tmp = mask;
                for (int i = 0; i < v; i++)
                {
                    label[i] = tmp % 6 + 1;
                    tmp /= 6;
                }

                // Count distinct dominoes used
                bool[,] used = new bool[7, 7];
                int count = 0;
                for (int i = 0; i < e; i++)
                {
                    int a = label[eu[i]];
                    int b = label[ev[i]];
                    int lo = Math.Min(a, b);
                    int hi = Math.Max(a, b);
                    if (!used[lo, hi])
                    {
                        used[lo, hi] = true;
                        count++;
                    }
                }
                if (count > best) best = count;
            }

            Console.WriteLine(best);
        }
    }
}
